# `DfoBuilder::with_max_iterations`

[Back to `dfo::DfoBuilder`](../DfoBuilder.md)

Sets the iteration (generation) budget.

## Signature

```cpp
dfo::DfoBuilder dfo::DfoBuilder::with_max_iterations(std::int64_t max_iterations) const;
```

## What It Does

Sets `DfoOptions::max_iterations`. A positive value overrides the method's own iteration or generation limit; the run then ends `ReachedIterationBudget` if the method has not converged first. Zero keeps the method's own limit, which for Nelder-Mead, pattern search and MADS is a multiple of the number of variables.

## Parameters

`std::int64_t max_iterations`
: The budget; 0 keeps the default.

## Returns

A new builder with the change; the original is untouched.

## Practical Examples

### Example 1

A short run.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace dfo = pluss::subsp::math::optimization;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  const auto f = [](const Series &x) { return (x - 3.0).square().sum(); };   // minimum 0 at (3, 3)

  const dfo::DfoResult r = dfo::DFO::build(pluss::series::make({0.0, 0.0})).with_objective(f).with_max_iterations(3).solve();
  out.writeln(dfo::to_string(r.status), ", iterations =", r.diagnostics.iterations, ", minimum =", r.minimum);
}
```

### Example 2

More iterations, a better answer.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace dfo = pluss::subsp::math::optimization;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(6));
  const auto rosenbrock = [](const Series &x) {
    const Series a = x.select(0, 0), b = x.select(0, 1);
    return (b - a * a).square() * 100.0 + (1.0 - a).square();
  };

  for (const std::int64_t n : {5, 20, 80}) {
    const dfo::DfoResult r = dfo::DFO::build(pluss::series::make({-1.2, 1.0})).with_objective(rosenbrock).with_max_iterations(n).solve();
    out.writeln("iterations", n, ": minimum =", r.minimum);
  }
}
```

### Example 3

For a population method the unit is a generation.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace dfo = pluss::subsp::math::optimization;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  const auto f = [](const Series &x) { return (x - pluss::series::make({1.0, -2.0, 0.5, 3.0})).square().sum(); };   // minimum 0 at (1, -2, 0.5, 3)

  const dfo::DfoResult r = dfo::DFO::build(pluss::series::make({0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0})).with_objective(f)
                               .with_solver(dfo::DfoSolverKind::ParticleSwarm).with_max_iterations(10).solve();
  out.writeln(dfo::to_string(r.status), ", generations =", r.diagnostics.iterations, ", evaluations =", r.diagnostics.evaluations);
}
```

